        },
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $T$ be the closure of the positive geometric two-strand braid $\\sigma_1^3$, with orientation given by increasing braid parameter. In the chart $(x,y,t)$ with ambient orientation $(x,y,t)$, view along $+y$, put increasing $t$ downward, and orient the projection plane by $(\\partial_t,\\partial_x)$. The right-starting strand passes over the left-starting strand at each positive crossing. Let $E_T$ be its chosen exterior. For the positive meridian $\\mu=a$ at the first left arc and the preferred degree-one longitude $\\lambda$, the fundamental group of $+1$ filling, with slope $[\\mu]+[\\lambda]$, has presentation\n$$\\pi_1(E_T(1/1))\\cong\\langle a,b\\mid aba=bab,\\;bab^{-1}aba^{-2}=1\\rangle.$$\nIn these based coordinates the blackboard parallel is $w=bac$ with $c=b^{-1}ab$, and\n$$w a^3=(ab)^3,\\qquad\\lambda=w a^{-3}=(ab)^3a^{-6}.$$\nThus the same filling relation is $(ab)^3=a^5$. In particular the positive trefoil and the sign of the filling are both fixed; no mirror substitution is implicit."
      }
